From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Omarchybot
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 14:37:45 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 29/29] Create /dev/nvidia-modeset at boot on NVIDIA machines

nvidia-utils' 60-nvidia.rules runs only `nvidia-modprobe -c0 -u`, so nothing creates the modeset node until something on the host opens the NVIDIA driver for display. On a hybrid laptop whose panel hangs off the iGPU that may never happen, and games under umu's Steam Runtime container or Flatpak then fail Vulkan presentation: the container cannot run the setuid helper, and Flatpak only binds the node if it existed when the sandbox was built.

Install the rule the reporter proved on their machine, gated like the packaged one so a GPU bound to vfio-pci is left alone. The setup leaf replays the bind because an image's first boot runs it after coldplug; the migration replays it only while the node is missing, so a retry after a failed udevadm still creates it and another user's run is a no-op.

Fixes #15975

Upstream: omacom/omarchy#16379 (open), its three commits efd6483cb,
dcdd06b8c and 1768b566d squashed, taken as is.

Backport to v4.5.0-rc2: install/hardware/nvidia.sh ends in our patch
0012's hybrid branch (no early load on hybrids), so the rule's install and
the bind replay go after that if/else instead of after the heredoc; the
lines are upstream's.

Co-Authored-By: Maciej Szostak <3469221+szoniu@users.noreply.github.com>
Co-Authored-By: Codex Medium <noreply@openai.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 default/udev/nvidia-modeset.rules |  5 +++++
 install/hardware/nvidia.sh        |  6 ++++++
 migrations/1792737693.sh          | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 27 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 default/udev/nvidia-modeset.rules
 create mode 100644 migrations/1792737693.sh

diff --git a/default/udev/nvidia-modeset.rules b/default/udev/nvidia-modeset.rules
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..06e1fffb9
--- /dev/null
+++ b/default/udev/nvidia-modeset.rules
@@ -0,0 +1,5 @@
+# nvidia-utils' 60-nvidia.rules never runs nvidia-modprobe -m, so /dev/nvidia-modeset can be missing on hybrid laptops,
+# and Steam Runtime and Flatpak containers can neither create it nor see one made after they started.
+ACTION=="add|bind", ATTR{vendor}=="0x10de", ATTR{class}=="0x03[0-9]*", \
+  DRIVER=="nvidia", TEST!="/dev/nvidia-modeset", \
+  RUN+="/usr/bin/nvidia-modprobe -m"
diff --git a/install/hardware/nvidia.sh b/install/hardware/nvidia.sh
index 226b1184b..1e4fa1f20 100644
--- a/install/hardware/nvidia.sh
+++ b/install/hardware/nvidia.sh
@@ -54,4 +54,10 @@ EOF
   else
     rm -f /etc/mkinitcpio.conf.d/nvidia.conf
   fi
+
+  # Create /dev/nvidia-modeset at boot, so containerized games can present on hybrid laptops
+  install -Dm644 "$OMARCHY_PATH/default/udev/nvidia-modeset.rules" /etc/udev/rules.d/61-nvidia-modeset.rules
+  # An image's first boot runs this after coldplug, so replay the GPU's bind for the new rule
+  udevadm control --reload 2>/dev/null || true
+  udevadm trigger --action=bind --subsystem-match=pci --attr-match=vendor=0x10de --attr-match='class=0x03*' 2>/dev/null || true
 fi
diff --git a/migrations/1792737693.sh b/migrations/1792737693.sh
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..b497c77ac
--- /dev/null
+++ b/migrations/1792737693.sh
@@ -0,0 +1,16 @@
+echo "Create /dev/nvidia-modeset at boot, so containerized games can present on hybrid NVIDIA laptops"
+
+rule=/etc/udev/rules.d/61-nvidia-modeset.rules
+
+if omarchy-hw-nvidia && ! omarchy-hw-aarch64-n1x && omarchy-cmd-present nvidia-modprobe; then
+  if ! cmp -s "$OMARCHY_PATH/default/udev/nvidia-modeset.rules" "$rule"; then
+    sudo install -Dm644 "$OMARCHY_PATH/default/udev/nvidia-modeset.rules" "$rule"
+  fi
+
+  # Replayed until the node exists, so a retry after a failed udevadm still creates it and another user's run is a no-op
+  if [[ ! -e /dev/nvidia-modeset ]]; then
+    sudo udevadm control --reload
+    sudo udevadm trigger --action=bind --subsystem-match=pci --attr-match=vendor=0x10de --attr-match='class=0x03*'
+    sudo udevadm settle
+  fi
+fi
-- 
